  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is not continuous at<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is everywhere differentiable",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is continuous but not differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is not differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msubsup><mo>|</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHD</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHD</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;not differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
